                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Time to go up, then down, up, up, sometimes down and up again.\r\n\r\nThat is essentially what the Surfingers experience is, taking your surfer across various layouts controlling waves so that they align to the next one or avoid an emerging obstacle. Whether that makes you a water deity is up to interpretation and you will need to pull those powers fast as waves come at you at a progressively quicker pace. Moreso, waves change for every run so you are not able to memorize them (outside of layout transitions), sometimes requiring you to double (or triple) tap in either direction.\r\n\r\nWith that in mind, the challenge looks daunting at the time of seeing achievements that go up to 500 points when each passed wave only gives you 1. However the practice comes as the star collectibles give one a way to unlock new characters outside of highscores. Furthermore, not all characters start in the same layout, making for an interesting tactic to try out which distribution suits you better from the start. Add that to changes in the screen resolution for better anticipation or maybe using 2 fingers instead of 1 depending on your coordination.\r\n\r\nBe as it may, the background tropical rock melody may start to wear you out at one point only to come back as an earworm with every new personal best (speaking from experience).",
